+# TeaseScript AI — ChatGPT project agent
+
+This ChatGPT project folder is a compact startup and acquisition layer. GitHub
+repository `TeaseScript-AI/teasescript-platform` is authoritative after a
+verified checkout exists. Do not treat this file, the research archive, or an
+older source artifact as current implementation authority.
+
+## Project boundaries
+
+Build a browser-first community platform and TeaseScript language for
+deterministic interactive teases, BDSM scenes, persistent personalities,
+roleplay adventures, and community packages. Source code, identifiers,
+TeaseScript keywords, APIs, comments, documentation, package metadata, editor
+text, and website UI use English.
+
+Keep these accepted boundaries unless current repository authority says
+otherwise:
+
+- Laravel with PostgreSQL is the only public backend.
+- Parser/runtime code is TypeScript compiled to JavaScript.
+- Regular executable content uses `.tease`; reusable advanced code uses real
+  TypeScript in `.ts`; `main.tease` is the package entry point.
+- Keep one deterministic engine, state model, and save/checkpoint format.
+- Runtime behavior that survives pause/resume uses validated versioned JSON-safe
+  plans and explicit state, not a suspended JavaScript call stack. JSON-safe
+  instruction boundaries do not require persisting after every instruction.
+- Player and package code run inside a sandboxed cross-origin iframe and have no
+  unrestricted external network access.
+- Start mobile as a responsive PWA. Do not add microservices, Kubernetes, Redis,
+  WebRTC, Electron, or native apps without a documented need and decision.
+
+## Project-folder inventory
+
+Keep no more than these five current unsuffixed files:
+
+```text
+README-FIRST.md
+teasescript-chatgpt-project-agent-tools-linux-x64.tar.zst
+teasescript-chatgpt-project-agent-runtime-linux-x64.tar.zst
+setup-teasescript-chatgpt-project-agent.py
+TeaseScript-AI-Research-Archive.zip        # optional non-authoritative research
+```
+
+The ChatGPT project system prompt is stored canonically in GitHub but belongs in
+the separate project-instructions field, not in this folder or either archive.
+Remove numbered, versioned, or superseded current copies instead of overlaying
+or manually merging them.
+
+## Install the local tools
+
+Use the direct shell/container executor. Do not wrap ordinary archive, Git,
+shell, Node, or npm commands in a notebook merely to invoke the shell.
+
+```bash
+python3 /mnt/data/setup-teasescript-chatgpt-project-agent.py
+```
+
+The installer verifies the exact outer archive digests recorded below, validates
+archive paths, file types, links, manifests, checksums, platform compatibility,
+and conflicts, then atomically exposes:
+
+```text
+/mnt/data/teasescript-chatgpt-project-agent/
+```
+
+Use `--replace` only to replace an existing valid installation after the new
+payloads have been fully validated and assembled.
+
+<!-- TEASESCRIPT_CHATGPT_PROJECT_ARTIFACTS_V1
+{{ARTIFACT_METADATA_JSON}}
+TEASESCRIPT_CHATGPT_PROJECT_ARTIFACTS_V1 -->
+
+## Obtain and prepare exact source
+
+For substantial implementation, review, debugging, or verification:
+
+1. Resolve the exact GitHub head and merge base and download the matching
+   verified Source Bundle artifact once.
+2. Run the installed normal entry point:
+
+```bash
+/mnt/data/teasescript-chatgpt-project-agent/bin/prepare-chatgpt-project-workspace.sh \
+  --artifact /mnt/data/source-bundle.zip \
+  --artifact-sha256 <github-artifact-sha256> \
+  --expected-head <40-character-head-sha> \
+  --expected-merge-base <40-character-merge-base-sha> \
+  --expected-repository TeaseScript-AI/teasescript-platform \
+  --output /mnt/data/source-work
+```
+
+3. In the verified checkout, read its `README-FIRST.md`, applicable `AGENTS.md`,
+   assigned issue or pull request, `CURRENT-DESIGN.md` for broad architecture,
+   `PHASE-STATUS.md` for current gates/status, and only the controlling task
+   documents and accepted ADRs.
+   Unless a later accepted ADR or explicitly recorded post-V30 owner decision
+   supersedes a specific point, `docs/specifications/accepted-syntaxes-v30.md`
+   remains the accepted syntax and semantics baseline.
+4. Use local Git, search, editing, and tests. Return to the connector only for
+   live GitHub state and writes.
+
+Do not network-clone from a connector-restricted agent, read the repository file
+by file through the connector, execute the candidate source-preparation helper
+from the artifact under review, invent a separate bootstrap self-test, or revive
+the removed work-package route.
+
+## Work and publication
+
+Use one coherent issue, one owner, one short-lived branch, one pull request,
+independent review, CI, squash merge, and branch deletion by default. Before
+substantive edits state expected files, acceptance criteria, and risks. Do not
+silently alter architecture, semantics, security boundaries, or scope.
+
+Immediately before a repository write choose either normal authenticated Git or
+the verified patch-publication route from the checkout's
+`docs/PATCH-PUBLICATION.md`. Publish generated binary files through that normal
+route without inventing a separate project-visible transport artifact.
+
+## Timeouts for known long actions
+
+Set an explicit extended tool timeout *before* starting aggregate local-agent
+validation, `npm run check`, workspace preparation with `--check`, or archive
+generation/compression. Normally allow at least 120 seconds for aggregate
+checks, and more when measured compression or CI-equivalent work requires it.
+Do not rely on a short default timeout and then repeat the same command.
+
+## Codex routing
+
+Choose the lowest-cost executor likely to produce an accepted result, including
+handoff, retries, review corrections, CI, and publication cost:
+
+- Keep work with a ChatGPT project agent when repository reading, review,
+  architecture, diagnosis, or existing-session context dominates.
+- Prefer Codex when direct `git`/`gh` materially reduces publication friction or
+  a bounded implementation is strongly verifiable.
+- Luna: mechanical/localized work with explicit edits and strong checks.
+- Terra: repository-aware implementation of fixed accepted boundaries.
+- Sol: unresolved architecture, canonical state/ordering/serialization design,
+  difficult nonlocal diagnosis, or independent semantic audit.
+
+Select reasoning separately: Low for deterministic work, Medium for bounded
+repository exploration/integration, High only for unresolved strategy or subtle
+cross-boundary diagnosis. The verified checkout's current workflow and model
+routing sources override this compact startup summary.
+
+## Research boundary
+
+`TeaseScript-AI-Research-Archive.zip` is optional, separate, and
+non-authoritative. It may inform capability research but does not define current
+syntax, architecture, status, or implementation.
